      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Post-match review",
          "heading": "Quesada names kicking game among what failed in Springboks defeat",
          "body": "Speaking after the 66-7 defeat in Turin, head coach Gonzalo Quesada called the Springboks' first half one of the best recently, but was candid about Italy's own failings: the kicking game and clearance kicks did not work, and in some situations they put themselves under pressure. He pointed to positives, including defence against the driving maul and a partial second-half comeback until the 70th minute, when Italy had more ball. Captain Giacomo Nicotera said he was disappointed that Italy had not fully respected their values."
        },
