          "heading": "Rees-Zammit ends eight-Test tryless run in Wales' 28-21 win over Japan",
          "body": "Louis Rees-Zammit stepped over just before half-time, after Eddie James had created the space, ending an eight-Test run without a try. Tomos Williams then released Josh Adams for his second, and Wales were made to sweat when Japan's Shinya Komura scored four minutes from time to cut the gap to a single score. Steve Tandy's side still took the bonus point for a second win of the tournament."
        },
